<title>ETHIOPIA: Britain gives Ethiopia cash for schools, road.</title>
<headline>Britain gives Ethiopia cash for schools, road.</headline>
<dateline>ADDIS ABABA 1996-11-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain will give Ethiopia nearly $11 million to improve its education system and roads, according to agreements signed on Saturday in the Ethiopian capital Addis Ababa.</p>
<p>British Overseas Development Minister Lynda Chalker and Ethiopian Education Minister Guenet Zewde and Planning and Economic Cooperation Minister Girma Biru signed the agreements.</p>
<p>Some $9.4 million will go towards a programme to improve elementary education in Ethiopia and $1.5 million towards a road project.</p>
</text>
